`append_hook_feedback_to_error`:
```rust
/// Append a failure hook's feedback to the tool's own error message, in the
/// same `[Hook feedback]` vocabulary the post path uses, **without ever
/// replacing the original reason** — the tool's error is the fact; the hook's
/// text is advice attached to it.
fn append_hook_feedback_to_error(err: ToolError, feedback: &str) -> ToolError {
    match err {
        ToolError::Failed(m) => ToolError::Failed(format!("{m}\n[Hook feedback]\n{feedback}")),
        ToolError::NotFound(m) => ToolError::NotFound(format!("{m}\n[Hook feedback]\n{feedback}")),
        ToolError::InvalidArgs(m) => ToolError::InvalidArgs(format!("{m}\n[Hook feedback]\n{feedback}")),
        // `Cancelled` carries no message, so there is nothing to attach
        // feedback to; the variant is a bare signal and is returned unchanged
        // rather than rewritten into `Failed`, which would change what the
        // cancellation *is*.
        other => other,
    }
}
```

Good. That's honest and simple.

