Let me design:

```rust
impl HookPhase {
    /// Every phase, in config-key order. **The single source of truth** for the
    /// accepted `hooks.<phase>.<tool>` spellings: the parser, the `/hooks`
    /// listing, the project-trust refusal message and the unknown-phase
    /// warning all read this rather than copying the set.
    pub const ALL: [HookPhase; 3] = [Self::Pre, Self::Post, Self::PostFailure];

    /// The config-key spelling. One spelling everywhere.
    pub fn as_str(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::Pre => "pre",
            Self::Post => "post",
            Self::PostFailure => "post_failure",
        }
    }

    /// Parse a config-key phase segment, or `None` if unknown.
    pub fn parse(s: &str) -> Option<Self> {
        Self::ALL.into_iter().find(|p| p.as_str() == s)
    }
}
```

